#!c=3600
`c`!`F2c8How to join ScotMesh Chat`f`!
`a
-
There's one conversation, #scotmesh, and three ways into it. Everyone sees the same messages whichever they use.

>This page
Read without doing anything. To post, identify yourself to this node (the fingerprint button in MeshChatX, or "Identify when connecting" in NomadNet), then reload.

>An LXMF messenger
From Sideband, MeshChatX, NomadNet or Columba, send `!/join`! to `!625ad393ca4df62a1382f9d936322a0a`!. Messages arrive like any conversation, as "Name: message". Send /help there for commands.

>An RRC client
In MeshChatX, NomadNet, rrc-tui or WeeChat, connect to hub `!004e5a15da221d9a236b0e8d74195f13`! and join `!scotmesh`!. When you reconnect you get what was said since you left.

>Names
Your name is tied to your Reticulum identity and is the same everywhere. Nobody else can take it or a lookalike of it. Free it with /forget, or on `F5af`_`[Your name & settings`:/page/me.mu]`_`f.

>Commands
The same commands work everywhere: here in Say, in the LXMF group and in the RRC room. Start them with / or !, which also works in NomadNet's RRC screen. Type /help to see them.

